,"where the sand hums like a great drum in the afternoon heat","where whole villages have been buried by a single storm","whose ridges are shaped like crescent moons","glowing rose-pink at dawn and deep red at dusk","where camel trains follow ridges known only to their guides","whose sandstorms can last a week","where every footprint is gone by morning","with no rock, no tree and no water for a hundred miles","where the dunes rise and fall like ocean waves","said to hide a lost city beneath its deepest dune","where travellers cross at night and shelter by day","whose star-shaped dunes can be seen from the mountains","where the sand is so fine it flows like water","crossed only by a nomad clan who never stays in one place","where sand-rays glide just below the surface","whose dunes boom like thunder when the sand slides","where the horizon looks the same in every direction","with sand the colour of honey and cinnamon","where guides read the wind like a map","whose highest dune has never been climbed"],"badlands":{"salt":["a blinding white salt pan that cracks into hexagons","where the dry lake bed mirrors the sky after rain","where salt miners work by night to escape the glare","the bed of a sea that vanished long ago","whose salt crust rings like glass underfoot","scattered with the fossils of giant sea creatures","where the ground is too salty for any plant","where travellers carry salt home to sell in the markets","where nothing grows but thorn bushes and lichen","crossed by a single dusty trail and a line of telegraph poles","home to vultures, rattlesnakes and very little else","whose mirages fool even the oldest scouts","crossed by a railway that was never finished"],"land":["cut by deep gullies and crooked canyons","where rock spires stand like a stone army","whose striped cliffs show every colour of rust and cream","where outlaws hide in a maze of buttes","where flash floods carve new canyons every spring","where the heat shimmers until the hills seem to float","whose mesas are topped with the ruins of cliff forts","where the wind howls through rock arches","where prospectors still dig for silver in the gullies","whose hoodoos glow orange in the evening light","where a sudden rain turns the clay to sticky mud","where nothing grows but thorn bushes and lichen","crossed by a single dusty trail and a line of telegraph poles","home to vultures, rattlesnakes and very little else","whose mirages fool even the oldest scouts","crossed by a railway that was never finished"]},"cursed":["where the dead walk when the moon is full","said to be cursed by a queen who was buried alive","where no bird flies and no beetle crawls","whose winds carry the voices of lost travellers","where an army vanished without a trace","haunted by a caravan that never reaches the oasis","where the sand is grey as old ash","whose ruins are guarded by restless spirits","where wells give only bitter water","where shadows move when there is no sun","whose dunes hide the tombs of forgotten tyrants","where travellers hear their names called in the night","said to be the grave of a god","scattered with the bones of great beasts","whose sandstorms leave behind strange footprints","where the sun burns pale and cold","where jackals howl from every ridge","whose oasis is said to grant a wish, at a terrible price","where black glass crunches underfoot","whose sky is always the colour of a bruise","where the old kings sleep under a curse","where even the wind seems to whisper warnings"],"scifi":["a desert world where colonists harvest water from the night air","with dust storms that cover the whole planet for months","whose glass plains were made by an ancient war","a mining colony on the edge of a red dwarf's glow","where the ground is too hot to walk on at noon","whose oceans dried up a million years ago","home to a lonely outpost and a trading post for smugglers","where cities are built deep underground to escape the heat","with a sky the colour of rust and three small moons","where solar farms stretch as far as the eye can see","whose sand is rich in rare crystals","where scavengers pick over the wrecks of old starships","a frontier world where water costs more than fuel","where terraformers gave up halfway through","home to burrowing creatures the size of trains","where the wind sings through towers of glassy rock","whose only city sits around a deep, ancient well","whose orbit takes it too close to its sun every winter","where hover-bikes race across the dry seabeds","whose ruins hint at a civilisation that vanished","a prison planet where the desert is the wall","whose settlers wear masks against the fine red dust","where water is mined from comets and shipped down by rocket"]}}}